# ───────── per-project frags ─────────
# Repos in ~/code/ can self-register an HTTPS proxy by dropping a
# `caddy.frag` file at their root. Use this for ephemeral, external,
# or not-yet-canonical projects — canonical long-lived projects stay
# in this template + PORTS.md.
#
# Example: /home/eldar/code/myrepo/caddy.frag
#   jarvis.<tailnet>.ts.net:1XXXX {
#     import tls_jarvis
#     reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:XXXX
#   }
#
# After adding/removing a frag: `sudo systemctl reload caddy`.
import /home/eldar/code/*/caddy.frag
